<title>Manage Credentials</title>
<context ID_FILE_MANAGE_CREDENTIALS IDD_MANAGE_CREDENTIALS />

The <b>Manage Credentials</b> dialog can be accessed from within the CSPro Designer, CSEntry, and Data Manager. On Android, managing credentials is done via the <link CSPro::android_settings.csdoc>Settings</link> menu option.


The dialog shows credentials related to:

<list>
    <li><b>Synchronization Services</b>: Credentials for <link CSPro::sync_services.csdoc>synchronization services</link>, including access tokens for <link CSPro::syncconnect_function_csweb.csdoc>CSWeb</link> and <link CSPro::syncconnect_function_dropbox.csdoc>Dropbox</link>, and passwords to <link CSPro::syncconnect_function_ftp.csdoc>FTP servers</link>.</li>
    <li><b>Encrypted Data</b>: Credentials for <link CSPro::data_source_csdbe.csdoc>Encrypted CSPro DB</link> data sources.</li>
    <li><b>Locations</b>: Cached locations used for <link CSPro::mapping.csdoc>mapping</link>.</li>
</list>


A single credential can be cleared by selecting it and pressing the <b>Clear</b> button. A group of credentials can be cleared by clicking the same button while selecting the heading for the credential type. Alternatively, the <b>Clear All</b> button can clear all credentials, or only synchronization or data credentials.


<seealso CSPro::android_settings.csdoc />
